# CODEOWNERS for 4thtech/agentlink: the S2 gate (decision D-25).
#
# The `main` ruleset requires a code-owner review, with 0 required approvals otherwise. A pull
# request that touches a path below therefore merges (or auto-merges) only after an approving
# review by @talirezun or @denisjazbec who is not its author. Pull requests are opened under
# @talirezun's account, so agent-built S2 work needs @denisjazbec's GitHub approval. A review
# relayed in chat does not satisfy it. Paths not listed here have no code owner.
#
# Listed: the S2 path defaults of docs/process/audit-rules.md §2.2, plus CI and release
# configuration, the supply-chain files that execute code (package.json, pnpm-workspace.yaml,
# .npmrc, .pnpmfile.*) and the agent rules. Keep this list, audit-rules.md §2.2 and the class rules in
# .github/workflows/review-gate.yml in sync. Content-rule S2 changes on other paths
# (audit-rules.md §2.4) are caught by review-gate, not here.
#
# Changing this file is itself code-owned (/.github/) and an owner-only decision.

# S2: crypto, keys, owner presence, envelope/pairing protocol, policy engine
/packages/crypto/                               @talirezun @denisjazbec
/packages/core/                                 @talirezun @denisjazbec
/packages/node/                                 @talirezun @denisjazbec

# S2: owner console, cloud agent (seeds), submitter (gas keys)
/apps/console/                                  @talirezun @denisjazbec
/apps/cloud-agent/                              @talirezun @denisjazbec
/apps/submitter/                                @talirezun @denisjazbec

# S2: canonical protocol vectors and the invariants
/test-vectors/                                  @talirezun @denisjazbec
/docs/foundation/04-security-and-crypto.md      @talirezun @denisjazbec

# CI, release and repository configuration (incl. this file, review-gate and release workflows)
/.github/                                       @talirezun @denisjazbec

# Supply-chain configuration that can run code or redirect installs and publishing in CI: the root
# manifest, pnpm workspace settings, .npmrc and pnpm hook files (.pnpmfile.cjs/.mjs), which pnpm
# executes and which could otherwise reach a job holding the npm OIDC token. No leading slash on
# the last two: they apply at any depth, like the class rule in review-gate.yml.
/package.json                                   @talirezun @denisjazbec
/pnpm-workspace.yaml                            @talirezun @denisjazbec
.npmrc                                          @talirezun @denisjazbec
.pnpmfile.*                                     @talirezun @denisjazbec

# Agent rules and harness settings
/AGENTS.md                                      @talirezun @denisjazbec
/CLAUDE.md                                      @talirezun @denisjazbec
/.claude/                                       @talirezun @denisjazbec
